    "narrative": "The **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jackson Merrill** tandem headlines today\u2019s rotation as our strongest plays, posting elite efficiency scores of 83.29 and 71.41 respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a high-upside matchup against L\u00f3pez, carrying a significant platoon advantage and prime placement in the three-hole, while **Jackson Merrill** faces Junk in a contest where his dynamic platoon edge and favorable spot in the order are primary drivers. **Drake Baldwin** also emerges as a key contributor at 72.68; his score is buoyed by an ideal park factor (+16%) and a high xwOBA against Baz, cementing his role as a must-start catcher despite the volatility of the position.\n\nTactical adjustments across the board leverage specific environmental and situational variables. **Denzer Guzman** (53.14) receives a notable boost from wind blowing out, helping mitigate a difficult matchup against Whisenhunt, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (66.25) remains a high-floor start despite a stiff test against the 3.58 xERA of Suarez, as his ability to handle left-handed pitching compensates for the wind blowing in. Conversely, **Kyle Tucker** (59.07) and **Andy Pages** (56.75) are both suppressed by poor BvP histories against Peralta, but their high base projections keep them safely in the starting outfield. The most difficult decision on the bench involved **Jorge Polanco**, who missed the cut at 45.79; while he provides reliable utility, the superior efficiency and platoon-adjusted upside of **Dominic Smith** (62.31) against Baz ultimately locked him into the OF3 spot.\n\nManagement must remain vigilant regarding risk factors today, particularly regarding **Heliot Ramos** (56.33). While he benefits from favorable wind, his efficiency is capped by the presence of an elite catcher for the opposition, which historically suppresses stolen base attempts\u2014a category we are prioritizing heavily today. We will be monitoring the lineup status of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Nasim Nunez** closely; both are currently projected for the bottom third of the order against Drake, and any further demotion in the lineup could result in a significant drop in their already marginal 5x5 utility.",
